es.","q":false},{"lap":0,"text":"Chiron made a good start from the second row to overtake all except Gaupillat, who held on to the lead from the Monegasque","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":11},{"lap":1,"text":"When the field appeared again Gaupillat was still leading having done the lap in 3m48s (128.7 km/h). He was followed by Chiron, Williams, Wimille and Lehoux.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":11},{"lap":1,"text":"Lehoux retires with a damaged rear axle; Bussienne and Bouriat both stop, Bouriat for 1m50s.","q":false,"c":18},{"lap":2,"text":"Light rain begins; Chiron takes the lead from Gaupillat with a 3m47s lap, and Williams and Wimille also pass Gaupillat.","q":false,"c":0},{"lap":3,"text":"The rain however did not hinder Chiron from putting in a new lap record on the third lap with a time of 3m46s (129.8 km/h).","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":0},{"lap":4,"text":"Mme Mareuse stalls at Val Gosset unable to find a gear; she gets away again and hands the car to Leygonie at the pits.","q":false,"c":14},{"lap":5,"text":"Chiron overshoots at Val Gosset and reverses back, dropping to third behind Williams and Wimille; a fast stop for goggles costs two more places.","q":false,"c":0},{"lap":8,"text":"On the eighth lap Wimille went off the road at Val Gosset but was able to rejoin the race without losing much time.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":13},{"lap":10,"text":"After 10 laps Williams leads in 39m31s, Wimille four seconds behind and Chiron 39 seconds further back; Howe leads the 2-litre class from Czaykowski.","q":false,"c":1},{"lap":10,"text":"Amilcar's head driver Jos\u00e9 Scaron retired his car with transmission problems and Max Fourny retired his Bugatti after having struck clutch problems.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":16},{"lap":11,"text":"Wimille's carburettor catches fire near St. Aubin; he jumps out of the car at speed, escaping with cuts and bruises.","q":false,"c":13},{"lap":12,"text":"De Maleplane makes a lengthy stop for repairs.","q":false,"c":17},{"lap":14,"text":"Williams holds a half-minute lead over Chiron, who chases him in the rain.","q":false,"c":1},{"lap":15,"text":"Williams laps in 3m45s, a new record.","q":false,"c":1},{"lap":16,"text":"Chiron replies with 3m43s.","q":false,"c":0},{"lap":17,"text":"Williams lowers the record again to 3m41s.","q":false,"c":1},{"lap":18,"text":"After the first hour Willimas was leading Chiron by half a minute and both had lapped the rest of the field.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":1},{"lap":25,"text":"After 25 laps the situation remained unchanged for the top trio. Bouriat, who had lost the bonnet of his Bugatti and was running with the engine fully visible, was now up to fourth followed by the 2 liter cars of Czaykowski and Howe.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":2},{"lap":26,"text":"Gaupillat hands his car to Lehoux; it refuses to start, and once sent back out Lehoux soon has to retire it.","q":false,"c":11},{"lap":28,"text":"Zehender had a moment at Val Gosset and then came slowly into the pits to retire, with gearbox problems. Charles Druck also retired, leaving 10 cars in the race.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":12},{"lap":34,"text":"Williams makes his routine stop, 56.8s; Chiron leads for the moment.","q":false,"c":1},{"lap":36,"text":"Chiron stops for 64.6s and loses more ground to Williams.","q":false,"c":0},{"lap":43,"text":"The rain stops and Chiron closes in; after 2h50min the gap is down to 21 seconds.","q":false,"c":0},{"lap":45,"text":"Williams goes wide at Val Gosset, losing six seconds; the gap is 11 seconds.","q":false,"c":1},{"lap":51,"text":"With 45 minutes left Chiron goes round two backmarkers on the outside at Maison Blanche, chasing Williams.","q":false,"c":0},{"lap":52,"text":"Chiron took the lead at Val Gosset but \"Williams\" retook it when Chiron went wide and up the the sandbank at St. Aubin. At Maison Blance it was \"Williams\" time to go wide and Chiron was back in the lead and started to pull away.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":0},{"lap":54,"text":"Williams, trying too hard to keep up, goes off into a ditch between Val Gosset and St. Aubin; he loses over two laps before rejoining with suspect steering and damaged brakes.","q":false,"c":1},{"lap":62,"text":"Four hours are up: Chiron wins, Williams second some 12 minutes back, Bouriat third, Czaykowski fourth and first in the 2-litre class, Howe 3 1/2 minutes behind him.","q":false,"c":0}]}